WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
1. Submit a repair request
The live member form creates this booking. Triage routes the pump repair to the $75 test deposit.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
2. Deposit required
The app shows Awaiting deposit. No visit time has been assigned.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
3. Pay in Stripe sandbox
Submitted sample test-card details through hosted Checkout. No real funds or saved payment method.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
4. Verify the payment result
Stripe sends checkout.session.completed with livemode=false. The app shows the $75 deposit receipt.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
5. Approve in Telegram
Pressed the actual Approve button on this booking. Audit actor: owner:telegram.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
6. Approval is separate from scheduling
The app shows Approved · time pending and keeps the paid test-deposit receipt.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
7. Assign the visit window
Sent /schedule for October 25, 2026, 2–3 PM EDT. Telegram confirms the saved window.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
8. Verify the scheduled app
The app shows Confirmed and the same 2–3 PM EDT visit window. Airtable holds the same UTC bounds.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000
9. Complete the visit in Airtable
Checked mark_completed on the same record. The writeback changes confirmed to completed.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.000
10. Verify completion in the app
The app now shows Completed. The $75 Stripe test payment remains recorded.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.000
11. Verify the completion notification
Telegram receives confirmed → completed for the same booking and visit window.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
12. Save a completion note
Entered a fictional completion note in Airtable. The visit_notes writeback is logged as applied.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
13. Verify Service history
The exact note appears under Repair in Service history. This completed request is no longer open.
